A2FPGA Multicard Core — Licensing
=================================

A2FPGA combines code written for this project with open-source cores from
other authors. Its licensing is therefore layered. The license header in
each file is authoritative for that file; this document explains how the
pieces fit together.

1. Code written for this project
--------------------------------

Files authored for A2FPGA that do not state a different license in their
header are made available under the MIT License (full text below). These
files may be reused in other projects under MIT terms on their own.

2. Third-party code
-------------------

Files from other authors retain their original authors' licenses, as
stated in their headers. Most are under permissive (MIT/BSD-style)
licenses. The following components are licensed under the GNU General
Public License (full texts in the LICENSES/ directory):

  - hdl/support/via6522.vhd — VIA 6522 core, Gideon Zweijtzer
    (1541ultimate project), GPL-3.0
  - hdl/support/TMS5220.vhd — TMS5220 speech chip core, d18c7db,
    GPL-3.0-or-later
  - hdl/support/iir_filter.v (and board-local copies) — audio IIR
    filter, Sorgelig (MiSTer project), GPL-2.0-or-later
  - boards/a2mega/hdl/twgs/65C816/ — 65C816 CPU core by srg320
    (SNES_MiSTer project), GPL-3.0
  - hdl/disk/hdd_rom.a65 — ProDOS HDD controller firmware, adapted from
    AppleWin, GPL-2.0-or-later
  - gcr_dsk.c in the BL616 and ESP32 firmware trees — 6-and-2 GCR
    codec ported from AppleWin, GPL-2.0-or-later

3. Combined works
-----------------

Each board's complete logic design incorporates one or more of the GPL
components above, so every A2FPGA bitstream — and any MCU firmware image
built with the AppleWin-derived GCR codec — is a combined work that is
conveyed, as a whole, under the GNU General Public License version 3
(see LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt). The corresponding source is this repository,
including the build scripts needed to rebuild and reflash each board.

The MIT license on A2FPGA-authored files is GPL-compatible: you may
still take those individual files into other projects under MIT terms.
If you build a design from this repository that includes any of the GPL
components, your combined design is subject to the GPL.

Board schematics and PCB design work created for this project are
independent works and are not derived from the GPL components above.

If you reuse any code from this project, check the header of each file
you take to confirm that your intended use is covered.

